The August 26 tsunami-like flooding – triggered by a rock-ice avalanche along the Nepal-China border – has killed more than 1,300 people, with roughly 5,000 others still missing. On Friday, the Nepal Army rescued two local workers trapped inside a hydropower tunnel for nine days, while a Chinese national was pulled out the following day.

